						 <div class="note"> <div style="text-align: center;"> <p>I hope that you've enjoyed my tale<br /> I hope it finds you well;<br /> If I write one more verse of rhyme<br /> I think I'll go to hell;<br /> But honestly it's been a slice,<br /> I hope your holidays are nice;<br /> Don't forget, you're the best,<br /> Keep hanging on;<br /> Please remain in quarantine!</p> </div> </div> <p>I've been made to feel very welcome during this, my first year on the site. Looking forward to continuing to get to know you all better, and no matter what this time of the year means to you — I'm an atheist, so it means family, food and commercialism to me, and so I'm staying in with my dad, eating whatever he got from the grocery store last week, and not spreading disease like a goddamn sollipsist — I hope it works out for you in some respect.</p> <p>Here's to next year.</p> <p><strong>Citation:</strong> The &quot;Huron Carol&quot; was written in Wyandot in 1642 by Jean de Brébeuf; using his melody (which was adapted from a French folk tune) Jesse Edgar Middleton wrote the English lyrics in 1926, and they entered the public domain in 2011. (Music copyright lengths are fucking stupid.) My version is, obviously, my own.</p> <p>All images are the author's, released under CC 3.0.</p> 
